<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<figure id="A0.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.22638v1/t2i-demo.png" id="A0.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/227;" width="548" height="227" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span><span id="A0.F4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Learning from mixed captions in text-to-image generation.</span>
During training, models learn from realistic image-caption pairs such as “<em id="A0.F4.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">a banana and an apple on the table</em>” or “<em id="A0.F4.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">a man surfing on an ocean wave</em>”. They can leverage language priors to recombine these captions and generate novel concepts, such as “<em id="A0.F4.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">a banana surfing on the ocean</em>” (images shown are generated with Gemini 2.5 Flash Image). By analogy to Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Language Models Can Learn fromVerbal Feedback Without Scalar Rewards" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, this illustrates how diverse verbal feedback can be treated as a conditioning signal, motivating our feedback-conditional learning paradigm.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Additional derivations and discussions</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Eq. (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.1 Offline training: Initializing feedback-conditional policy ‣ 2 Learning directly from verbal feedback ‣ Language Models Can Learn fromVerbal Feedback Without Scalar Rewards" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and its special case</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al. (2023)</a></cite>, the optimal solution to a KL-constrained reward maximization problem <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\log p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})\right]-\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}\left(\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})||\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\log p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})\right]-\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}\left(\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})||\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\pi^{*}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})&amp;=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot\exp\left(\log p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})\right)}{\sum_{\bm{o}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot\exp\left(\log p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})\right)}\\
&amp;=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}{\sum_{\bm{o}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}\\
&amp;=\frac{P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}},{\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}})}{P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}})}=P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})\textrm{.}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\pi^{*}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})&amp;=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot\exp\left(\log p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})\right)}{\sum_{\bm{o}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot\exp\left(\log p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})\right)}\\
&amp;=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}{\sum_{\bm{o}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}\\
&amp;=\frac{P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}},{\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}})}{P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}})}=P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})\textrm{.}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that the objective in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.1 Offline training: Initializing feedback-conditional policy ‣ 2 Learning directly from verbal feedback ‣ Language Models Can Learn fromVerbal Feedback Without Scalar Rewards" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) is equivalent to minimizing the <em id="A1.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">reverse</em> KL divergence between <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\!\!\left[\log p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})\right]-\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}\!\left(\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})||\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\right)\\
={}&amp;-\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}\!\left(\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})||P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})\right)+\log P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}})\textrm{.}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>env</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.552em;" width="0.552em"><mi>𝔻</mi></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.552em;" width="0.552em"><mi>𝔻</mi></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\!\!\left[\log p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})\right]-\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}\!\left(\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})||\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\right)\\
={}&amp;-\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}\!\left(\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})||P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})\right)+\log P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}})\textrm{.}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In the special case where the environment provides <em id="A1.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">verifiable rewards</em>, that is, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}}^{+})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}}^{+})=1</annotation></semantics></math> for correct responses <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{o}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{o}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}}^{-})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}}^{-})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for incorrect responses <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{o}}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{o}}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can show that <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to the optimal solution of a 0-1 reward maximization problem without KL regularization: <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})\in\arg\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})\in\arg\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. Specially, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})&amp;=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}^{+}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}}^{+})}{\sum_{\bm{o}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}^{+}|{\bm{x}})}{\sum_{{\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})}\textrm{;}\\
P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}^{-}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})&amp;=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}^{-}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}}^{-})}{\sum_{\bm{o}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}=0\textrm{.}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>;</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})&amp;=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}^{+}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}}^{+})}{\sum_{\bm{o}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}^{+}|{\bm{x}})}{\sum_{{\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})}\textrm{;}\\
P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}^{-}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})&amp;=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}^{-}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}}^{-})}{\sum_{\bm{o}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}^{+}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}=0\textrm{.}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus, taking <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})=P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})=P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})</annotation></semantics></math> into the formula of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})\right]=\sum_{{\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+}}\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})}{\sum_{{\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})}=1\textrm{.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟙</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})\right]=\sum_{{\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+}}\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})}{\sum_{{\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+}}\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})}=1\textrm{.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Since there is <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})\right]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})\right]=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})=P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})=P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})</annotation></semantics></math> is one of the optimal solutions (not unique), i.e., <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})\in\arg\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>off</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒐</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\textrm{off}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})\in\arg\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\pi({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}}^{+})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{o}}\textrm{ is }{\bm{o}}^{+})\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Connection to inverse dynamics modeling</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In traditional RL, objectives for representation learning are often grouped into three classes: <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> behavior cloning</span>, <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">forward dynamics</span>, and <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">inverse dynamics</span>. Behavior cloning is typically used for imitation learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arora et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, forward dynamics is central to world modeling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ha &amp; Schmidhuber, 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schwarzer et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, and inverse dynamics has been explored for both pretraining <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Brandfonbrener et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and feature extraction for exploration in RL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Efroni et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Interestingly, analogous structures appear in the LLM literature. The objectives of supervised finetuning (SFT), critique finetuning (CFT) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>, and our feedback-conditional policy (FCP) align naturally with behavior cloning, forward dynamics, and inverse dynamics, respectively:</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\textbf{SFT (behavior cloning):}&amp;\quad\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\right]\textrm{;}\\
\textbf{CFT (forward dynamics):}&amp;\quad\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\mathbb{E}_{p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}\left[\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{c}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})\right]\right]\textrm{;}\\
\textbf{Our FCP (inverse dynamics):}&amp;\quad\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\mathbb{E}_{p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}\left[\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}})\right]\right]\textrm{.}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">SFT (behavior cloning):</mtext></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>;</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">CFT (forward dynamics):</mtext></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>;</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Our FCP (inverse dynamics):</mtext></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>env</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒄</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\textbf{SFT (behavior cloning):}&amp;\quad\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})\right]\textrm{;}\\
\textbf{CFT (forward dynamics):}&amp;\quad\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\mathbb{E}_{p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}\left[\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{c}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})\right]\right]\textrm{;}\\
\textbf{Our FCP (inverse dynamics):}&amp;\quad\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\mathbb{E}_{p_{\textrm{env}}({\bm{c}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{o}})}\left[\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{o}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{c}})\right]\right]\textrm{.}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We further illustrate this categorization with graphical models in Figure <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ A.2 Connection to inverse dynamics modeling ‣ Appendix A Additional derivations and discussions ‣ Language Models Can Learn fromVerbal Feedback Without Scalar Rewards" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. This unified perspective clarifies the conditional structure underlying each finetuning paradigm and highlights how different forms of supervision drive model learning. In particular, our FCP extends the analogy by treating verbal feedback as a first-class supervision signal, positioning it as the natural <em id="A1.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">inverse-dynamics</em> counterpart to existing finetuning objectives.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A1.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.22638v1/BC-SFT.svg" id="A1.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/380;" width="548" height="380"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>SFT (<em id="A1.F5.sf1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">behavior cloning</em>)</figcaption>
